## Context

The LP matcher (`src/aedist/matching/lp.py`, `DEFAULT_SIMILARITY_THRESHOLD = 90`
at line 70) uses `rapidfuzz.fuzz.partial_ratio >= similarity_threshold` (line 220)
to decide fuzzy matches. Review item 0534#6 asked for a false-match estimate on
phase-named plants (e.g. Vũng Áng 1 vs Vũng Áng 2), where partial_ratio is
structurally high across phases. The item was waived twice (#968, #971) because no
committed artifact backed a number; the source-concordance table caption
(`slides/manuscript/main.tex` ~line 1315) says percentages are "upper bounds" with
no quantification.

Key finding from Imagine phase: the LP already has a unit-number veto
(`lp.py` lines 203–208) — when both names carry digit tokens that differ, cost is
set to `2*dummy_cost+1`, making cross-phase assignment structurally impossible in
the LP. Equivalent guard in `matching/phased.py` `_digit_compatible()` (line 17).
The ticket is therefore a **documentation-artifact exercise**: measure and commit
the structural false-match set (pairs the veto blocks) and the realised cross-phase
rate from run outputs (which is zero at threshold 90, confirmed from the existing
`experiments/derived/matching_sensitivity.csv`). The sensitivity data already
exists: F1 is identical at thresholds 75–90 (`n_fuzzy_below = 0`), drops ~0.046
mean at threshold 95.

