## Actions

1. **New script** `src/aedist/analyze_matcher_phase_collisions.py`:
   - `argparse` entry point; `logging`, no hardcoded paths
   - CLI flags: `--reference PATH` (default `VN_THERMAL_PLANTS_RELEASE_CSV`),
     `--sensitivity PATH` (default `experiments/derived/matching_sensitivity.csv`),
     `--output-csv PATH` (default `report/inputs/generated/tab_phase_collisions.csv`),
     `--output-macros PATH` (default `report/inputs/generated/macros_phase_collisions.tex`)
   - Load reference via `load_plants_csv(VN_THERMAL_PLANTS_RELEASE_CSV)` from
     `aedist.evaluate`
   - Compute all-pairs partial_ratio matrix using `rapidfuzz.process.cdist`
     (177×177, not a hand-rolled nested loop)
   - For each threshold in [85, 90, 95]: the **structural false-match set** =
     all pairs of distinct plants where `score >= threshold` (raw exposure of the
     threshold itself — Vũng Áng 1/2 belongs here, per the original ticket test).
     Each pair carries a `veto_blocked` boolean: True when both names have digit
     tokens and they differ (the LP veto would fire, lp.py:203–208). The
     non-blocked subset is the **residual exposure** the LP could actually pick.
   - CSV columns: `name_a,name_b,partial_ratio,threshold,veto_blocked`
   - Read `matching_sensitivity.csv`, compute per-threshold mean F1 and sum of
     `n_fuzzy_below` across all runs at each threshold (85/90/95)
   - Emit `macros_phase_collisions.tex` with these macros (follow
     `macros_source_concordance.tex` naming style — PascalCase nouns):
     - `\PhaseCollisionPairsNinety` — structural pairs ≥ 90 (raw exposure, incl. veto-blocked)
     - `\PhaseCollisionVetoBlockedNinety` — of those, blocked by the unit-number veto
     - `\PhaseCollisionResidualNinety` — not veto-blocked (residual exposure)
     - `\PhaseCollisionPairsEightyFive` / `\PhaseCollisionPairsNinetyFive` — raw exposure at 85 / 95
     - `\RealisedFuzzyBelowNinety` — total `n_fuzzy_below` at threshold 90 across
       all runs (expected: 0)
     - `\ThresholdSensFOneDropNinetyFive` — mean F1 drop from threshold 90 to 95,
       expressed as a decimal to 3 places (e.g. `0.046`)

2. **Wire into render.mk** after the concordance rule (after line ~890), following
   the same grouped-target `&:` pattern:
   ```make
   $(ANALYSIS_GEN)/tab_phase_collisions.csv \
   $(ANALYSIS_GEN)/macros_phase_collisions.tex &: \
       $(ANALYSIS_EXPERT_REF) \
       $(ANALYSIS_REPO_ROOT)/src/aedist/analyze_matcher_phase_collisions.py \
