       uv run python -m aedist.analyze_matcher_phase_collisions \
           --output-csv $(ANALYSIS_GEN)/tab_phase_collisions.csv \
           --output-macros $(ANALYSIS_GEN)/macros_phase_collisions.tex
   ```
   Check whether `ANALYSIS_EXPERT_REF` is defined in paths.mk or render.mk; if not,
   substitute the literal variable that resolves to
   `data/reference/vietnam_thermal_plants_v2_classified.csv`.

3. **Add `\input` to main.tex preamble** (after the existing `\input` at line 1631
   or near preamble macro-include area — follow the single existing `\input` pattern):
   ```latex
   \input{../../report/inputs/generated/macros_phase_collisions.tex}
   ```
   Asset path is relative to `slides/manuscript/` per tectonic convention.

4. **Edit concordance caveat** in `main.tex` ~line 1315: replace "so the
   percentages are upper bounds" with a sentence that cites
   `\PhaseCollisionPairsNinety` (raw exposure), `\PhaseCollisionResidualNinety`
