## Test

File: `tests/test_analyze_matcher_phase_collisions.py`

**First red test (write before implementing):**

```python
@pytest.mark.parametrize("name_a,name_b,in_set,veto_blocked", [
    # Vũng Áng 1 vs 2: high partial_ratio across phases — MUST appear in the
    # structural false-match set at t=90 (original ticket red test), and MUST
    # be flagged veto_blocked=True (digit tokens differ → LP veto fires)
    ("vung ang 1", "vung ang 2", True, True),
    # A same-plant pair: never in the set (distinct-plants guard)
    ("vung ang 1", "vung ang 1", False, None),
])
def test_structural_set_and_veto_flag(name_a, name_b, in_set, veto_blocked):
    from aedist.analyze_matcher_phase_collisions import structural_false_matches
    pairs = structural_false_matches(threshold=90)  # {(a, b): veto_blocked}
    key = (name_a, name_b) if (name_a, name_b) in pairs else (name_b, name_a)
    assert (key in pairs) == in_set
    if in_set:
        assert pairs[key] == veto_blocked
```

Anti-tautology requirements: the Vũng Áng case is the original ticket's red
test (set must be non-empty and contain it at t=90). Additionally assert at
least one veto_blocked=False pair if the residual set is non-empty on the real
reference (derive the pair from the generated CSV after implementing, then
hardcode it); if the residual set is empty at t=90, assert that instead —
either way the test pins both sides of the veto flag.

